    <!-- T-DNS-LOCK: hide the Private DNS Settings UI row.
         PrivateDnsPreferenceController.getAvailabilityStatus():87-94 reads
         R.bool.config_show_private_dns_settings and returns UNSUPPORTED_ON_DEVICE
         when false, hiding the row AND de-indexing it from Settings search.
         AOSP default is true (packages/apps/Settings/res/values/config.xml:401).

         This is the UI-hiding half of T-DNS-LOCK. The enforcement half —
         forcing Settings.Global.private_dns_mode="hostname" (3),
         private_dns_specifier="dns.guardtalk.io", and
         private_dns_default_mode="hostname", plus the
         DISALLOW_CONFIG_PRIVATE_DNS user restriction (a DEVICE_OWNER-only
         restriction per UserRestrictionsUtils.java:203-208, settable only by
         a SYSTEM_UID process or device owner) — is deferred to T-GTCONFIG-APP,
         the platform-signed privileged GuardTalkConfig system_ext app
         (vendor/guardtalk/apps/GuardTalkConfig), which already holds
         WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS + MANAGE_USERS. The dispatch packet explicitly
         permits this follow-up path ("If too complex for this task, document
         it as a follow-up for T-GTCONFIG-APP"). The .io TLD (not .local) is
         used because .local fails strict DoT validation.

         Mechanism chosen for the defaults (documented for T-GTCONFIG-APP):
         Settings.Global.putString(PRIVATE_DNS_MODE, "hostname"),
         putString(PRIVATE_DNS_SPECIFIER, "dns.guardtalk.io"),
         putString(PRIVATE_DNS_DEFAULT_MODE, "hostname") on first boot via a
         BOOT_COMPLETED receiver in GuardTalkConfig. No init.rc / sysprop path
         exists for Settings.Global rows (they are not sysprops), and the
         SettingsProvider defaults.xml does not seed private_dns_* keys
         (verified: no def_private_dns_* resource exists). -->
    <bool name="config_show_private_dns_settings">false</bool>

